# The derived index. Disposable by ADR-0003: deleting it costs a rebuild.
.kb/

# The private layer. Gitignored by design, because it is nobody's to publish.
profile/
records/
projects/

# Transcripts fetched for this agent, which are two things at once: derived by
# ADR-0003, because the recording they came from is the source of truth and the
# text is a projection of it, and usually somebody else's words rather than ours.
# Tracked is our notes and a citation; ignored is their words.
#
# Only this folder, and not `inbox/` itself. An inbox already holds the agent's
# own notes awaiting distillation, and bases like zed and yaron keep a typed
# structure in it with a `what-goes-here.md`. Ignoring the whole inbox would take
# the structure out with the payload, which is the opposite of the intent.
#
# SOURCES.md is the exception that makes the rest honest: ignoring a derived file
# is only safe when what it was derived from is written down. Without the ledger
# a fresh clone cannot regenerate a transcript and cannot even say what used to
# be here, so "derived, therefore disposable" would be a claim with nothing
# behind it. The folder and its ledger are created on the first ingest.
inbox/transcripts/*
!inbox/transcripts/.gitkeep
!inbox/transcripts/SOURCES.md
